<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59952" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTD/445/59952.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2012" href="schedule/2012.xml">2012</calendarYear><term id="120128" href="schedule/2012/fall.xml">Fall 2012</term><subject id="ARTD" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTD.xml">Art--Design</subject><course id="445" href="schedule/2012/fall/ARTD/445.xml">Seminar in Design</course></parents><sectionNumber>GRD</sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: "The Experience of Meaning in Design" explores what actually occurs when we humans process text and image. It is a complicated and compelling issue. The course will connect students to design-relevant literature in psychology, education, and literary theory. In this traditionally-structured seminar, students will supplement weekly readings with short position papers, writing exercises, and occasional exploratory work.  Graduate Section.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2012-08-27Z</startDate><endDate>2012-12-12Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>07:40 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>319</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Peterson" firstName="M">Peterson, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>